    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1298">

                <pb facs="0885" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/43.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Vice Consul Davis.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1914</hi></date>,</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>If attempt is made to impose forced loans on Americans, you will make formal
                    protest.</p>
                <p>However, in case authorities persist in attempt to collect, advise Americans to
                    pay under protest, making protest a matter of record if possible, and to take
                    receipts for amounts paid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
